{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "035E", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-birational-over-normal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:61bba225f2ddb2b66785fe7c409a1c675333698b96442afc3143ad7a4bd3a769", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6a13f5738094ba00d2551da7f5277867f249d6865049474e00e44681214c8885", "source_text": "A finite (or even integral) birational morphism <MATH_0001>\nof integral schemes with <MATH_0002> normal is an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a9046a7f835df9c5fa6b873bdd590da630f17dbffe6926cf81614fdc5a8e9dd4", "unit_id": "tag:0AB1:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "035E", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$V \\subset Y$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y(V) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$Y$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y(V)$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y(V)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y(V) = \\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0011": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:14041f184372f5a1780a1d799c899bd418943dd829a898d1414c3da5fbf18dd1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d1a6efdca8a2f0b10190167bef223df2eef06c1778be3af509f73c667c497590", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine open\nwith inverse image <MATH_0002> which is an affine open too.\nSince <MATH_0003> is a birational morphism of integral schemes, the homomorphism\n<MATH_0004> is an injective map of domains\nwhich induces an isomorphism of fraction fields. As <MATH_0005> is normal,\nthe ring <MATH_0006> is integrally closed in the fraction field.\nSince <MATH_0007> is finite (or integral) every element of <MATH_0008>\nis integral over <MATH_0009>. We conclude that\n<MATH_0010>. This proves that <MATH_0011> is an\nisomorphism as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:91747c9a01743c84511de0cf554adfd31dbc1a4b498398a4135ccf8dfe70bbb2", "unit_id": "tag:0AB1:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "035E", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\nu : X^\\nu \\to X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-normalization-trivial}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:80977bd40a3896ce591c2cb6c9ae097a2b02789f67803138cc8a78bc22718ff0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5ae4d3ef8e77e593b61770920663889d9ab576fd65b18f4552d5ded118008b56", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme with locally finitely many irreducible components.\nThe normalization morphism <MATH_0002> is an isomorphism\nif and only if <MATH_0003> is normal.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9bbd9958b455b8bdd11effab99b230e66e751a177c53b016177e7342d691ddaa", "unit_id": "tag:0H7D:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "035E", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\nu$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\nu$", "MATH_0006": "$X^\\nu$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-normalization-normal}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-normalization-localization}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{properties-lemma-normal-locally-finite-nr-irreducibles}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-normalization-normal}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-normalization-birational}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-finite-birational-over-normal}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9725a947d358786d7ada0313063609b5cfa6160ce3fafb1a3d000840d890426d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d0caa80c86c76988d1d3ef2e6bb470a70dd6086e3f509cfa971f60333af27806", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is an isomorphism, then <MATH_0002> is normal by\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nConversely, suppose <MATH_0003> is normal.\nBy Lemma <REF_0002> and\nProperties, Lemma <REF_0003>\nwe may assume <MATH_0004> is integral.\nBy Lemma <REF_0004> the morphism\n<MATH_0005> is integral and <MATH_0006> has a unique irreducible component\n(so it is an integral scheme).\nWe conclude from Lemmas <REF_0005> and\n<REF_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ec968a4fd7930ae94e1ff5c41a9ef8f7384be46fe690dda487286d7c71c4800d", "unit_id": "tag:0H7D:proof"}
